WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:08.500
This is Charm City Pulse: free help, alerts and city services for everyone in Baltimore, on any phone, in English and Spanish.

2
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:20.851
The Today page puts what matters first. It reads live weather, air quality and city alerts, and says plainly what to do, like limiting time outside on a dangerously cold morning.

3
00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:34.182
If someone is in trouble, Get help now is one screen of big buttons: call nine one one, find a bed tonight, get directions to the closest warm place, or reach two one one for food and rent help.

4
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:46.723
My block answers everything about one address: your trash and recycling days, bulk pickup, street sweeping, whether you're near a snow emergency route, and how to reach your council member.

5
00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:55.103
The map brings it all together: snow emergency routes, trash days, libraries with free Wi-Fi, and warming centers.

6
00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:05.381
Get help also explains renters' rights in plain words, including free lawyers for people facing eviction, and help with rent, lead paint and rats.

7
00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:17.389
For city staff, the City brief ranks all fifty-five neighborhoods and fourteen council districts on heat, shade, health and social vulnerability, and shows who lives far from help.

8
00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:22.381
It can also answer a planning question: what if we opened a center here?

9
00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:31.509
Tap a spot, and it shows how many residents would newly live within a mile, and how many of them are in the city's highest-need areas.

10
00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:37.695
Any neighborhood gets a printable, one-page brief for meetings and community groups.

11
00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:44.291
It's free, it updates itself every day, and it's live now. Try Charm City Pulse today.
